course: dictionary
lesson: 7064
title: One word, many paths
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word path has more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one. Read the words around it and ask: what would fit here? A path can be a narrow way to walk on, a route that something moves along, or a plan for the future.
explain: «Children who leave the path and lose sight of their group get lost quickly, because trees all look alike.» The clues are leave, lose sight and trees, so path means a narrow way to walk on. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: «A barge is a long flat boat on a canal; here a horse walking on the tow-path pulls it.» The brackets tell you the tow-path is the path beside the canal. Brackets, dashes and commas often explain a word, so look for them.
explain: When the clues are not clear, use a dictionary. A career path is a way of working through your life, not a path you walk on, so the context and your check must match.
fact: A path is a narrow way to walk on, through a park, garden or woods.
fact: A path can also be the line or route along which something moves, such as the path of a ball or the path of a storm.
fact: A path can be a way of living or a plan for the future, as in «a career path».
fact: Check the words around path: the clues in the sentence tell you which meaning is right.
fact: «Grit or sand sprinkled on an icy path gives shoes more grip.» Here path means a walkway you can stand and walk on.
exercise: «Children who leave the path and lose sight of their group get lost quickly, because trees all look alike.» What is a path in this sentence? | A plan for the future | *A narrow way to walk on | The line a ball follows | A flat boat on a canal
exercise: «Grit or sand sprinkled on an icy path gives shoes more grip.» Why is grit put on the path? | *To give shoes more grip | To make the path colder | To turn the path into a road | To paint the path a new colour
exercise: The weather forecast showed the path of the storm across the coast. What does path mean here? | *The route along which the storm moves | A narrow way through the woods | A flat boat on a canal | A plan for a new job
test: «A barge is a long flat boat on a canal; here a horse walking on the tow-path pulls it with a long rope.» What is the tow-path? | The rope the horse pulls with | *The path beside the canal | The handle that steers the rudder | The boat that the barge-woman steers
test: Sam says «a career path» means a path you walk in the park. What is a career path really? | A narrow way through the trees | A cycle lane beside the road | *A plan or way of working through your life | The line a ball travels along
exam: Which sentence uses path to mean a plan for the future? | «Chalk drawings belong on your own driveway or a quiet path.» | «The path of light bends.» | «The path of the Moon goes around the Earth.» | *«She chose a career path in medicine.»
